# Paths that git will not carry into a new worktree, because they are
# untracked or ignored, but the project needs anyway.
#
# scripts/new-worktree.sh symlinks each one back to the main checkout. That
# means the contents are SHARED with the main project, not isolated -- writing
# to a linked path from a worktree writes to the real thing.
#
# One relative path per line. Blank lines and "#" comments are ignored. A path
# that does not exist is reported and skipped, not created as a broken link.

